==========================================================================================
PART A: symbolic gamma->0 behavior of K(lambda,gamma)
==========================================================================================
lim_{gamma->0+} K(lambda,gamma) = -oo  (lambda fixed, positive)
CONFIRMED: unbounded (diverges to -infinity for lambda>0) as gamma->0+,
independently re-derived by direct sympy.limit on the closed form.

ln T_prof(lambda,gamma) = -ln(gamma) - ((2-gamma)/(2*gamma))*lambda^2
  -> already blows up at LEADING order (eps^0) as gamma->0; this is
     a property of T_prof itself (cited, Estagio 56), not of K. The
     eps^1-order K(lambda,gamma)'s own -lambda/gamma term is an
     ADDITIONAL, separate divergence on top of that, with no other
     gamma-dependent piece anywhere in K, Delta, or T_prof's OWN
     eps^1-order structure to offset it.

